# Supabase project (Settings > API in the Supabase dashboard > Connect >
# Framework > React). When configured, Supabase email/password is the real
# login source and authenticated shared business data loads from the staging
# application repository backed by the normalized CSV import/audit tables.
# Use the public anon/publishable key here, never a secret/service-role key.
# The Express host exposes these public values through /api/config at runtime;
# static-only hosting still needs them available during the Vite build.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Express server only: required for Admin account creation. Use a Supabase
# secret key (or the legacy service-role key) for the same project as the URL.
# Set in .env.local for local runs or server environment variables in hosting.
# Express loads Vite's mode-specific env files at startup. Restart after edits.
# Never add a VITE_ prefix. SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is also accepted for the
# legacy service-role key used by the import CLI.
# Static hosting and `npm run preview` do not provide this protected API.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Controls provenance for evaluations submitted through the application.
# Keep "staging" in test environments so those submissions never affect
# official Analytics. Set to "production" only in the approved live deployment.
VITE_DEPLOYMENT_ENV=staging

# Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) App Registration - required for real
# "Sign in with Microsoft" login and for sending partner report emails via
# Microsoft Graph (see src/services/msalAuth.ts and graphMailService.ts).
# Leave these blank when Microsoft login and Graph email are not configured.
#
# Setup steps (Azure Portal > Entra ID > App registrations > New registration):
#   1. Name it anything (e.g. "Supplier Management System").
#   2. Supported account types: "Accounts in this organizational directory only".
#   3. Redirect URI: platform "Single-page application (SPA)", value = the
#      exact URL this app is served from (e.g. http://localhost:3000 for dev,
#      and your production URL - add both as separate redirect URIs).
#   4. After creation, copy "Application (client) ID" and "Directory (tenant) ID"
#      from the Overview page into the two variables below.
#   5. API permissions > Add a permission > Microsoft Graph > Delegated:
#      add User.Read and Mail.Send. No admin consent is required for either
#      (both are standard delegated permissions) - each user just consents
#      for themselves on first sign-in.
#   6. No client secret is needed - this is a public client (browser-only,
#      delegated) flow, nothing server-side to secure.
VITE_AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_AZURE_TENANT_ID=
# Optional - defaults to window.location.origin if omitted.
VITE_AZURE_REDIRECT_URI=
